      "city_envelope": {
        "comment": "Authoritative, unambiguous definition of the wall polygon. Added 2026-07-23 because the prose description ('D-shaped semicircle' + 'northern chord wall at Z=4000' + 'curved southern wall r=500 centered (0,4500)') admitted two mutually incompatible readings: a full circle (whose bounds coincidentally match outer_bounds exactly, with Z=4000 as its tangent point rather than a chord) and a true D-shape. The D-shape is authoritative: it alone satisfies outer_bounds, the 'D-shaped' description, canon's semicircular-city-at-the-southern-edge, AND the district envelopes.",
